**thread.hpp creates, names, enumerates, suspends, and resumes Windows threads.**

## API

`set_name` overloads: `(HANDLE|DWORD|std::thread&|std::string) → bool`; `create_named_thread<Args...>(std::string, Args&&...) → std::thread`; `get_thread_ids() → std::vector<DWORD>`; `for_each_thread(std::function<void(HANDLE)>) → void`; `suspend_other_threads()`, `resume_other_threads() → void`.

## Contracts

`create_named_thread` forwards `Args...`, names the thread, and returns joinable `std::thread`; depends on `<thread>`, `nt.hpp`, `HANDLE`, and `DWORD`.